### SCENARIO 6 — tenant A does a day's work; tenant B then tries everything; tenant A is untouched.
###
### Both dispatchers hold the same role, the same scopes and the same rules. The only difference is
### the tenant their key was issued for, so anything B cannot do is tenancy and nothing else.
###
### It ends by re-reading tenant A's whole working set and comparing it, field by field, with what A
### left behind — because "B got a 404" is not the same claim as "A's data is intact". A write that
### was refused with the right status and applied anyway would pass the first and fail the second.

### Tenant A's session: a customer, two jobs, an update, and a read of its own set.
# @name ACreatesCustomer
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/customers
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}",
  "name": "Journey Holdings",
  "tier": "priority",
  "email": "ops@journey.test"
}

###
# @name ACreatesJob1
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}",
  "reference": "WO-8501",
  "title": "Journey job one",
  "status": "scheduled",
  "priority": 1,
  "quoted_price": 111.00,
  "internal_notes": "Tenant A only.",
  "access_code": "JOURNEY-1",
  "customer_id": "{{ACreatesCustomer.response.body.$.id}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}"
}

###
# @name ACreatesJob2
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}",
  "reference": "WO-8502",
  "title": "Journey job two",
  "status": "scheduled",
  "priority": 2,
  "quoted_price": 222.00,
  "access_code": "JOURNEY-2",
  "customer_id": "{{ACreatesCustomer.response.body.$.id}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}"
}

###
# @name AUpdatesJob1
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
PATCH {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{ACreatesJob1.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
If-Match: {{ACreatesJob1.response.headers.ETag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "in_progress", "quoted_price": 131.00 }

### What tenant A leaves behind, and the thing the end of this scenario compares against.
# @name ASetBefore
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?customer_id=eq.{{ACreatesCustomer.response.body.$.id}}&order=reference.asc&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### Tenant B's turn. It cannot SEE them.
# @name BListsWorkOrders
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?limit=100&order=reference.asc
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherSouth}}

###
# @name BListsCustomers
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/customers?limit=100&order=name.asc
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherSouth}}

### It cannot INFER them: a filter naming A's row narrows to nothing rather than refusing
# @name BFiltersForAsJob
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?reference=eq.WO-8501&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherSouth}}

### It cannot READ them
# @name BReadsAsJob
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [404]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{ACreatesJob1.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherSouth}}

###
# @name BReadsAsCustomer
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [404]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/customers/{{ACreatesCustomer.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherSouth}}

### It cannot MODIFY them
# @name BUpdatesAsJob
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [404]
PATCH {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{ACreatesJob1.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherSouth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "cancelled", "quoted_price": 1.00, "title": "Hijacked" }

### It cannot DELETE them
# @name BDeletesAsJob
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [404]
DELETE {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{ACreatesJob2.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherSouth}}

### It cannot condition a write on A's version either — a 412 would confirm the row exists, so the
### row-level exclusion has to be answered FIRST.
# @name BConditionsOnAsVersion
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [404]
PATCH {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{ACreatesJob1.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherSouth}}
If-Match: {{ACreatesJob1.response.headers.ETag}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "cancelled" }

### It cannot reach them through a reference from a row of its own
# @name BReferencesAsCustomer
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherSouth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantSouth}}",
  "reference": "WO-8601",
  "title": "Reaching across",
  "status": "scheduled",
  "priority": 1,
  "access_code": "CROSS",
  "customer_id": "{{ACreatesCustomer.response.body.$.id}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}"
}

### And it cannot place a row into A's tenant
# @name BCreatesIntoA
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [403]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherSouth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantNorth}}",
  "reference": "WO-8602",
  "title": "Planting",
  "status": "scheduled",
  "priority": 1,
  "access_code": "CROSS",
  "customer_id": "{{SouthCustomerId}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}"
}

### Tenant B's own session still works, so none of the above is B being broken
# @name BWorksInItsOwnTenant
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherSouth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{tenantSouth}}",
  "reference": "WO-8603",
  "title": "Tenant B's own job",
  "status": "scheduled",
  "priority": 1,
  "access_code": "OWN",
  "customer_id": "{{SouthCustomerId}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionNorthId}}"
}

### THE STATE OF THE WORLD: tenant A's set, re-read after everything above.
# @name ASetAfter
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?customer_id=eq.{{ACreatesCustomer.response.body.$.id}}&order=reference.asc&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name AsCustomerAfter
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/customers/{{ACreatesCustomer.response.body.$.id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
